<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A({2},\,{1},\,{1})</m>, <m>B({11},\,{7},\,{-8})</m> and <m>P({5},\,{3},\,{-2})</m> lie on one straight line.</p><div>(a) P divides AB [ internally | externally ]  </div><div>(b) <m>AP : PB =</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> <m>:</m> <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/>   </div><p>Give the ratio in whole numbers.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>\overrightarrow{AB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 9 \\ 6 \\ -9 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{AP} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 3 \\ 2 \\ -3 \end{array}\right)} = {\frac{1}{3}}\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>t = {\frac{1}{3}}</m> is between 0 and 1, so P is between A and B: P divides AB internally.</p><p>(b) <m>\overrightarrow{PB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 6 \\ 4 \\ -6 \end{array}\right)}</m>, which is <m>{\frac{2}{3}}\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>. So the lengths are in the ratio <m>AP : PB = {\frac{1}{3}} : {\frac{2}{3}} = {1} : {2}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>internally</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>